#. (itstool) path: sect2/title
#: C/index.docbook:7025
#: C/index.docbook:7025
msgid "History of Gnome Commander"
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7026
#: C/index.docbook:7026
msgid "Gnome Commander was primarily written by Marcus Bjurman, who was the one initiating this project in 2001 and developed it up to version 1.1.6 in January 2004."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7028
#: C/index.docbook:7028
msgid "Later on, since 2004, Gnome Commander was maintained by the new lead developer Piotr Eljasiak, working at the project already since 2002. In this time, Assaf Gordon contributed by implementing the internal file viewer."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7031
#: C/index.docbook:7031
msgid "Piotr conducted the development until version 1.2.8.15. In this time Magnus Stålnacke was responsible for the homepage. On the mailing list, amongst others, Michael and Magnus contributed with many great ideas and by helping finding bugs and other inconsistencies. After Magnus resigned from the project, Thomas Jost helped to maintain the homepage at Savannah.org"
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7036
#: C/index.docbook:7036
msgid "While the program was first written in C, Piotr started to migrate the codebase to C++. The migration was never really finished and the status was merely a mixture of both."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7039
#: C/index.docbook:7039
msgid "Unfortunately, Piotr suddenly passed away in the beginning of 2012 and Gnome Commander had no maintainer for nearly two years. Late in 2013, Uwe Scholz, a user of Gnome Commander since the days before version 1.0, took over the project as project maintainer. His main goal was to keep the project alive, e.g. by getting rid of the legacy library dependency \"gnome-vfs\"."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7044
#: C/index.docbook:7044
msgid "In 2024, Andrey Kutejko got involved in the project and migrated Gnome Commander from Gtk2 to Gtk4. He also started the migration from C++ to the Rust language."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7046
#: C/index.docbook:7046
msgid "In early 2026, Wladimir Palant joined the project and fixed a lot of bugs, improved performance and introduced new features, for example the embedded terminal output. Wladimir became the new project maintainer after the release of Gnome Commander version 2.0."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7052
#: C/index.docbook:7052
msgid "In the beginning, Gnome Commander had its home at Sourceforge. Later, the project moved to Savannah.org, where it got its own homepage and its mailing lists. In the end of 2003, the source tree moved to Gnome.org. Though, the homepage and mailing lists were still hosted at Savannah."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7056
#: C/index.docbook:7056
msgid "Since 2013, the location of the Gnome Commander home page has been moved to GitHub.org."
msgstr ""

#. (itstool) path: sect2/para
#: C/index.docbook:7057
#: C/index.docbook:7057
msgid "Since 2026, the location of the Gnome Commander home page has been moved to GNOME GitLab pages where it also got a modern outfit."
msgstr ""

